  "body": "Follow-up to #122299.\n\nAI-assisted: this maintainer-requested cleanup used Codex-backed implementation and review.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw still had a broad tail of locally reimplemented coercion bodies after the earlier consolidation rounds. Exact string, record, numeric, date, Boolean, CLI-argument, and error adapters were duplicated across core, plugins, packages, scripts, and UI. That made equivalent boundaries easy to drift and left ownership difficult to enforce mechanically.\n\nThis is round four of the explicitly requested coercion cleanup. It follows the semantic body scan after #122299 and consolidates only contract-exact implementations.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe patch resolves 87 exact string/record candidates: 85 migrate to their existing canonical owners, while two remain local because one script is copied standalone and one trusted current-tree harness runs against an old target working directory. It also migrates 61 numeric bodies, six date adapters, the compatible Boolean and CLI grammars, canonical-name collision families, and dense exact error clusters. It adds the hostile-input-safe `toStructuredErrorObject`, keeps dependency-light script argument helpers behind a matching runtime declaration companion, and removes deprecated internal text-runtime bypasses.\n\nThe ownership guard now covers 101 explicitly allowed declarations and a small direct-export completeness audit. Its earlier structural body mini-interpreter and implementation-coupled tests were removed under Repair Doctrine; the executable declaration inventory and focused export audit are the canonical enforcement path.\n\nCurrent-main overlap was preserved during rebase, including the explicit OpenAI provider selection, Telegram session-route owner, suite test-support classification, and Gateway session helper rename. No config, protocol, SQLite schema, dependency, version, release, or changelog surface changes.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThere is no intended user-visible behavior change. Maintainers get one smaller and more enforceable coercion surface, fewer local policy copies, and canonical hostile-error handling while existing call-site semantics remain unchanged.\n\nProduction/tooling changes are +1,132/-1,181 (net -49) before the 69-line dependency-light declaration companion. Tests and test support are +484/-482 (net +2). The complete 276-file patch is +1,685/-1,663 (net +22).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- Focused repository test wrapper: 9 files across four shards, 182 assertions passed. This includes canonical string/record/number/Boolean/error coercion, arg-utils, the 14/14 declaration guard, and 23 Diffs assertions.\n- `node scripts/check-changed.mjs --dry-run`: selected `lanes=all` and extension typecheck.\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kzt5fsp9p4ezk6gjyxe8mmx2`, Actions run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/31565107677:\n  - real `check:changed`: exit 0 in 15m23s;\n  - 101-declaration coercion guard, SDK API/exports/surface, deprecated API, package boundaries, dead exports, typecheck, lint, runtime cycles, and all planned guards passed;\n  - all four plugin boundary modes passed with zero violations;\n  - full build passed in 3m33s, including all 152 public Plugin SDK subpaths and Control UI;\n  - runtime-value and Madge cycles are zero;\n  - curated and full Diffs asset builds match committed bytes.\n- The prior `plugins:boundary-report:ci` red result was reproduced identically on the original clean base. Latest `main` independently removed the due compatibility record; the rebased exact head is green with `eligibleForRemoval=0`. No compatibility record was changed here.\n- Fresh frozen-head Codex-backed P2 autoreview: TruffleHog clean, one complete review pass, no accepted/actionable findings.\n- The first hosted exact-head run found the two missed standalone/historical harness boundaries. Both failures were root-caused to workspace-package resolution outside the workspace, both false migrations were removed, the exact two-file suite passed 17/17, and the final 440 KB exact-head P2 review is clean.\n- Final hosted pull-request CI: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/31567498198\n- Direct upstream Codex contract inspection confirmed the changed adapters against:\n  - `codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/v2/thread.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/v2/item.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/v2/mcp.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/app-server-protocol/src/protocol/common.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/app-server/src/bespoke_event_handling.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/app-server/src/request_processors/thread_processor.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/app-server/tests/suite/v2/compaction.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/app-server/README.md`\n  - `codex-rs/history/src/lib.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/rollout/src/recorder.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/protocol/src/openai_models.rs`\n  - `codex-rs/codex-api/src/endpoint/models.rs`\n\nNo release, version bump, npm publish, changelog change, protocol bump, SQLite schema-version bump, or dependency override is included.\n",
